<title>GERMANY: Hamburg air cargo volume falls 7.1pct in March.</title>
<headline>Hamburg air cargo volume falls 7.1pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Hamburg airport (HAM) in March fell 7.1 percent to 3,083 tonnes compared to the same month last year, figures from the German airports association ADV show.</p>
<p>Air cargo at Hamburg airport declined 3.9 percent in the first quarter of 1997, the monthly ADV traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The following tables give7 details with all figures in tonnes and percentage changes on the same period 12 months ago.</p>
<p>   March 1997	 Monthly total     Pct change</p>
<p>Total flown cargo     3,083		Down 7.1</p>
<p>Exports		   1,162		Down 10.5</p>
<p>Imports		   1,916		Down 4.5</p>
<p>Transit			 5		N.A.</p>
<p>   Jan-Mar 1997    Cumulative total   Pct change</p>
<p>Total flown cargo     8,723	    Down 3.9</p>
<p>Exports		   3,385	    Down 6.8</p>
<p>Imports		   5,327	    Down 1.5</p>
<p>Transit			11	    N.A.</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
</text>
